On Sun, 17 Aug 2014, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> My understanding is that if the level with the predetermined Ludios level
> number will be generated it will get the portal to Ludios (Knox is always
> virtually existent) generated iff the preconditions (like existing vault)
> will match. Do you object?

Absolutely.  The sourcecode src/mklev.c, function mk_knox_portal, holds
the rules and doesn't check against the hidden "bookkeeping" depth.

Note that Knox's hidden depth is always at least 18, but the portal can
occur as early as level 11.

Nethack also seems not to generate levels if you skip them with
levelport.  So if your first move after ^O is to ^V to the indicated
level, then you are boosting the chance that the portal will be there.
Normally deeper levels are less likely to have the portal, but this is
because normally you visit every upper level first.

